  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 1242 AM CDT Sat Aug 8 2026\n\nMonday the upper ridge will begin to shift back toward the \nsoutheast. Movement will be very slow, Monday will be very similar \nto Sunday. High temperatures will stay hot and near normal and a few \nspots in the Coastal Plains could briefly reach Heat Advisory \ncriteria. A few showers or thunderstorms could move over the Coastal \nPlains, but the inland advance will be limited by height rises to \nthe west. As the ridge continues to shift back toward the southeast, \nrain chances will come to an end Tuesday. Temperatures will creep up \na bit into the middle of next week. The higher temperatures combined \nwith the humidity may produce Heat Advisory criteria across the area \nsouth of I-10 and east of I-37.",
